        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Tsushima</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">27–28 May 1905</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Tsushima Strait, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsushima-island">Tsushima Island</a>, between the Japanese island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and the Korean Peninsula</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Japanese Combined Fleet under Admiral Tōgō Heihachirō, with over 40 vessels leading from the flagship Mikasa; the Russian Second Pacific Squadron under Admiral Zinovy Rozhestvensky, joined by the Third Pacific Squadron under Rear Admiral Nikolai Nebogatov, numbering 38 ships and outnumbered nearly three to one in total hulls</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">All 11 Russian battleships were lost, seven sunk and four captured. Russian dead were more than 5,000, and the Japanese lost no heavy ships and had 117 dead.</span></div>
